CORE
main.c
--dfcc main --replace-call-with-contract foo _ --dfcc main --replace-call-with-contract bar
^EXIT=6$
^SIGNAL=0$
^.*DFCC instrumentation has already been applied to this binary.*$
^.*Only one DFCC pass per binary is supported.*$
--
^.*VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL.*$
This test runs two pure --replace-call-with-contract DFCC passes, no
--enforce-contract on either invocation, on the same goto binary.
The second invocation must still fail with the per-binary DFCC error
message: the marker is set by *any* DFCC pass, not just contract
enforcement, and the new error wording reflects that.
